            <ArticleTitle>[Efficacy analysis of laparoscopic adjustable gastric placation for obesity].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>446-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To analyze the efficacy and safety of laparoscopic adjustable gastric placation (LAGBP), a new procedure for surgical treatment of obesity.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Clinical and 1-year follow-up data of 10 patients who underwent LAGBP in our department between September and November 2011 were analyzed retrospectively.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The mean operative time was (93.0±13.4) min, while the mean intraoperative blood loss was (15.5±4.7) ml. The mean excessive body weight loss rate(%EWL) at 3, 6, 9 and 12 months after the operation was 25.1%, 40.6%, 45.3% and 50.8% respectively. There were no severe post operative complications.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">LAGBP is associated with high safety and good short-term efficacy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
